{"path":"skills-next/comprehende/references/example.md","ref":"5f50618caf4f4029e5dbba2aa5e83419842b8460","side":"new","lines":[{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":1,"text":"# Example review.json"},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":2,"text":""},{"sha":"3031fcfc72737b521d526fa4e8d268ff208f3e41","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1792696630,"line":3,"text":"Optional filled sample. The field shape in `SKILL.md` is enough to write a document. Paths come from the `pregroup` draft, and so does `source`. When a file is split, `oldStart` and `newStart` come from that hunk's `@@` header."},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":4,"text":""},{"sha":"ee9f79a7d6790f4e36ca9f027a1c799c3b386ced","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790349567,"line":5,"text":"- `login` depends on `cookie`. Both use `part` \"Session cookie\". The helper's test sits in `cookie` with the helper it checks."},{"sha":"123b37bed0b9c4dafff5b5a187a0f73192913854","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787409379,"line":6,"text":"- `docs` is a separate part, last in `suggestedOrder`, because it could have been its own pull request."},{"sha":"c77e82775e65bb5e490a77688e8ffd272829c18f","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1789847074,"line":7,"text":"- Ticket #12 names why this work exists, so document `why` is present. Document `title` keeps the ticket title. Document `summary` names both stories. Document `parts` holds a one-sentence what per story. The why cites the ticket with `[#12](source:s1)`."},{"sha":"6284efe1e3e79fd1ca0ddb2c1454594f4f5ef7f8","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793515095,"line":8,"text":"- `login` `summary` names how those hunks meet. `cookie` has a `contract` attention with its predicted trace, and `login` a `product` call. `docs` has no attention."},{"sha":"6284efe1e3e79fd1ca0ddb2c1454594f4f5ef7f8","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793515095,"line":9,"text":"- Document `lookFor` compares ticket #12 with the diff: work the ticket asks for that no hunk does, and an item done differently. Both cite `[#12](source:s1)`."},{"sha":"6284efe1e3e79fd1ca0ddb2c1454594f4f5ef7f8","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793515095,"line":10,"text":"- A refactor idea (`parseCookie` could reuse `splitHeader`), a nit (`opts` is a vague name), and a missing test (expired cookies) are not in the document."},{"sha":"885f5d551634c9c40408bdb65f7fbd58a5b29134","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1792664421,"line":11,"text":"- Each group holds every hunk of its files, so each `hunkRefs` entry is a path. A split file uses `path@oldStart+newStart` (`old/path -> new/path@oldStart+newStart` when renamed). A directory of mechanical files the draft collapsed stays one `dir/` ref."},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":12,"text":""},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":13,"text":"```json"},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":14,"text":"{"},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":15,"text":"  \"version\": 1,"},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":16,"text":"  \"source\": {"},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":17,"text":"    \"baseRef\": \"origin/main\","},{"sha":"2cbb99191147fd1a87aad9563a4f103fd826b513","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1787288235,"line":18,"text":"    \"headRef\": \"HEAD\","},{"sha":"3031fcfc72737b521d526fa4e8d268ff208f3e41","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1792696630,"line":19,"text":"    \"range\": \"origin/main...HEAD\","},{"sha":"3031fcfc72737b521d526fa4e8d268ff208f3e